---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on NZSalary.com: What Is Set in Your Browser" description="Cookies and local storage on NZSalary.com: none for the calculators, Clarity and Google Analytics for statistics, no consent banner, and how to block them." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Cookies', path: route('cookies', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Cookies</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Does the pay calculator store anything?</h2>
    <p>No cookie, no local storage. Your pay, tax code and KiwiSaver rate live in the open tab; after you edit a field they also appear in the address bar, which is what lets you share a link to your result.</p>
    <h2>What do the statistics tools store?</h2>
    <p>Two analytics services write cookies. Microsoft Clarity, which turns visits into heatmaps and anonymous replays with typed values masked, keeps <code>_clck</code> for a year and <code>_clsk</code> for a day, and Microsoft can add <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. Google Analytics 4, from Google Ireland Limited, keeps <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_TEEYWPJZ4E</code> for two years each to count page views, referrers, time spent, engagement, device and rough location, and holds its reports for 14 months. Neither writes an advertising cookie.</p>
    <h2>How do I switch them off?</h2>
    <p>There is no pop-up asking for consent: both scripts run from the first page view. Your browser can stop them if you block third-party cookies or the <code>clarity.ms</code> and <code>google-analytics.com</code> domains, and Google publishes an <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">opt-out add-on</a> for Analytics. Delete the site’s data to clear cookies already written. PAYE, KiwiSaver and student loan results come out the same.</p>
    <p>Questions: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
